# The Windows CI runners set core.autocrlf in their system gitconfig, so a
# checkout there rewrites every text file to CRLF. win/src/ids.zig embeds
# win/src/resource.h and searches it for `#define NAME value\n`, and that
# search finds nothing in a CRLF copy. sh reads a trailing \r as part of a
# command, so scripts/*.sh need LF too.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.db binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary

Formula/ export-ignore
Casks/ export-ignore
bucket/ export-ignore
ports/ export-ignore
